SUMMARY:🌆🚶‍♂️ SUMMER EVENING WALK DOWN YONGE STREET & BEAVERTA
 ILS BY THE WATER 🍁🍩
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n🌆🚶‍♂️ SUMMER EVENING W
 ALK DOWN YONGE STREET & BEAVERTAILS BY THE WATER 🍁🍩\n\nToronto Light
 s\, City Energy & A Sweet Treat by the Lake\nThere is something special ab
 out Toronto on a summer evening.\nThe city is alive. Patios are full. Stre
 et performers are out.\n\nThe energy feels completely different once the s
 un starts to go down.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed social walk down one of the
  most famous streets in Canada as we make our way south along Yonge Street
  toward Toronto's beautiful waterfront.\n\nAlong the way we'll enjoy the s
 ights\, sounds\, and people-watching that make downtown Toronto so unique.
  From historic buildings and busy intersections to hidden corners of the c
 ity\, there's always something interesting happening on Yonge Street.\nThi
 s is not a historical tour.\n\nIt's a social walk focused on conversation\
 , meeting new people\, and enjoying a summer evening together.\n\nAnd of c
 ourse...\n\nWe'll finish with one of Canada's greatest inventions: BeaverT
 ails. 🍁😄\nAfter grabbing our treats\, we'll head down to the waterfr
 ont where we'll spend 30–40 minutes relaxing by the lake\, enjoying the 
 views\, and getting to know each other.\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:
 **[ Click here to join](https://chat.whatsapp.com/DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\
 n\n***\n\n🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll begin on Yonge Street and m
 ake our way south through the heart of downtown Toronto.\n\nAlong the way 
 we'll:\n🏙️ Walk through the city core\n📸 Stop for photos and inter
 esting sights\n😊 Meet new people and enjoy conversation\n🍁 Grab Beav
 erTails near the waterfront\n🌊 Relax by Lake Ontario for 30–40 minute
 s\n🌇 Enjoy the evening skyline and waterfront atmosphere\n\nThe total e
 xperience is approximately 2 hours depending on the pace of the group.\nYo
 u're welcome to leave at any time.\n\n***\n\n☀️ Weather & Expectations
 \n\nThis event will happen in typical summer weather conditions.\nThat mea
 ns sunshine\, clouds\, heat\, humidity\, or light rain.\n\nThe only reason
  we would cancel is for severe weather or thunderstorms.\nPlease dress com
 fortably and bring water if it's a warm evening.\nThis is a social walk\, 
 not a race.\n\nWe'll keep a comfortable pace that allows people to chat an
 d enjoy the city.\n\n***\n\n🧢 Meetup Details\n📍 Meetup Location: Out
 side the subway station\n🫎 I'll be wearing my Moose Hat\n⏰ Meetup Tim
 e: 6:30 PM\nI will only wait 5 minutes.\nEarly is on time.\nOn time is lat
 e.\n\nWe will leave promptly and won't be able to spend time tracking peop
 le down.\n\n🏁 End Point: Toronto Waterfront\n\n***\n\n🎟️ Meetup Fe
 e: $5 cash in person or e-transfer to\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](
 mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\n\nThis fee helps support the group an
 d allows us to continue organizing events like this. Thank you for support
 ing community! 💖\n\n***\n\n🎒 What to Bring\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfort
 able walking shoes\n🧥 Light sweater (optional for later in the evening)
 \n📸 Camera or phone for photos\n🍁 Money for BeaverTails\n\n***\n\n
 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis group is open to anyone who wants to be soci
 al and make friends — whether single or not.\n\nWe also host:\n🎬 Movi
 es\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Arts & culture outings\n🍽️ Restaurant ga
 therings\n\nThere's always something happening.\n\n***\n\nREMEMBER: You're
  welcome to just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\
 nAnd as always\, sometimes plans shift and events may need to be cancelled
  — please keep an eye on updates.\n\n***\n\n👤 Organizer: Mathew\nQues
 tions? Post on the event wall or email\n📧 [torontomoviesandoutings@hotm
 ail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)\n\nCome for the walk.
  Stay for the waterfront.\n\nLeave with sticky fingers\, a full stomach\, 
 and a few new friends. 🌆🍁✨
