SUMMARY:🌳🌿 EVENING HIGH PARK SUMMER WALK 🌿🌳
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n🌳🌿 EVENING HIGH PARK SUMMER 
 WALK 🌿🌳\n\nToronto's Biggest Park\, Hidden Trails & Great Company\nH
 igh Park is Toronto's largest and most beloved park — and once you start
  exploring it\, it's easy to understand why.\n\nFrom winding trails and fo
 rested paths to Grenadier Pond\, beautiful gardens\, historic landmarks\, 
 and even a small zoo\, High Park offers a little bit of everything. Despit
 e being right in the middle of the city\, parts of the park feel surprisin
 gly wild and peaceful.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed social walk as we explore 
 some of the best parts of High Park together.\n\nThis is not a historical 
 tour.\n\nIt's a social walk focused on fresh air\, exercise\, conversation
 \, and enjoying one of Toronto's most beautiful green spaces.\n\n**👉 Do
 n't forget to join our WhatsApp group – CLICK HERE!**\n\n***\n\n🚶‍
 ♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll spend approximately 2 hours exploring High P
 ark's trails\, pathways\, and scenic areas.\n\nAlong the way we'll:\n🌳 
 Walk through wooded trails\n🦆 Visit Grenadier Pond\n📸 Stop at some o
 f the park's most beautiful spots\n😊 Take a short break along the route
 \n🚶 Continue exploring before returning to the subway station\nPlease n
 ote there are several hills and a large staircase on this route.\nNothing 
 extreme\, but there are hills and stairs that you will be able to climb an
 d you should be comfortable walking for an extended period.\n\nThis walk i
 s suitable for most people with a moderate fitness level.\n\n***\n\n☀️
  Weather & Expectations\n\nThis event happens rain or shine.\nSummer weath
 er can change quickly\, so please dress appropriately and be prepared for 
 sun\, heat\, or light rain.\n\nThe only reason we would cancel is for seve
 re weather conditions.\nThis is a social walking group\, not a race.\n\nWe
 'll keep a comfortable pace while still moving steadily through the park.\
 n\n***\n\n🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 Meetup Location: High Park Sign (wes
 t side of Bloor Street and High Park Avenue)\n🫎 I'll be wearing my Moos
 e Hat\n⏰ Meetup Time: 11:00 AM\nI will only wait 5 minutes.\nEarly is on
  time.\nOn time is late.\n\n🏁 End Point: Back at High Park Subway Stati
 on\n\n***\n\n🎟️ Meetup Fee: $5 cash in person or e-transfer to\n📧 
 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\nThis fe
 e helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events like
  this. Thank you for supporting community! 💖\n\n***\n\n🎒 What to Bri
 ng\n💧 Water\n👟 Good walking shoes\n🥨 A snack\n🧴 Sunscreen\n
 🕶️ Sunglasses\n\n***\n\n🌈 Who Is This For?\nThis group is open to 
 anyone who wants to be social and make friends — whether single or not.\
 n\nWe also host:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Arts & culture out
 ings\n🍽️ Restaurant gatherings\nThere's always something happening.\n
 \n***\n\nREMEMBER: You're welcome to just show up on the day if you're uns
 ure about your schedule.\nAnd as always\, sometimes plans shift and events
  may need to be cancelled — please keep an eye on updates.\n\n***\n\n
 👤 Organizer: Mathew\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email\n📧 [
 torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmai
 l.com)
